<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 05:00:09 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Explosions shake Kyiv as US Congress advances new sanctions on Moscow</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-live-explosions-kyiv-us-congress-sanctions-moscow</link><description>
The US House on Wednesday passed a broad package of sanctions targeting Russian officials and key pillars of its economy as lawmakers look to deprive President Vladimir Putin of the financial resources needed to wage the war against Ukraine. Loud explosions were heard across Kyiv overnight on Wednesday into Thursday as authorities issued a missile alert, an AFP journalist reported. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/399ee18a-8287-11f1-beb6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2265621554.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/399ee18a-8287-11f1-beb6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2265621554.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8dcaad00-b23b-11f1-8f27-a733a75bb45c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 02:08:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/399ee18a-8287-11f1-beb6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2265621554.jpg">© Heather Diehl, Getty Images via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Putin urges Russians to vote in parliamentary election as show of support for Ukraine war</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-putin-urges-russians-to-vote-in-parliamentary-election-as-show-of-support-for-ukraine-war</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir ⁠Putin on Wednesday described voter turnout in the upcoming parliamentary election as a barometer of public support for Russia’s war against Ukraine and urged voters to go to the polls. It will be Russia's first parliamentary election since the Kremlin launched its offensive in February 2022.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d70c6b42-b200-11f1-8501-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259666126716.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d70c6b42-b200-11f1-8501-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259666126716.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e33974bc-b202-11f1-bc70-ab98b003be29</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:47:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d70c6b42-b200-11f1-8501-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259666126716.jpg">© Mikhail Metzel, Sputnik, Kremlin Pool Photo via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>LGBTQ 'a threat to Erdogan's ideal of a strong, masculine state', expert says</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/lgbtq-a-threat-to-erdogan-s-ideal-of-a-strong-masculine-state-expert-says</link><description>
Turkish courts have jailed more LGBTQ activists and supporters, raising to 62 the number remanded in custody following a weekend crackdown, a legal rights group said on Wednesday. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Koen Slootmaeckers, Reader in International Politics at City St George's, University of London, says that Turkish President Recep Tayyp Erdogan wants to claim "the idea of a strong, masculine state and LGBTQ people are a threat to this ideal".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8e0a398-b205-11f1-b9f2-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-210358-211115-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8e0a398-b205-11f1-b9f2-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-210358-211115-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">deb66500-b205-11f1-a1e9-135d799d52f5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:39:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sweden's centre-left opposition wins election, SVT says</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-wins-election-svt-says</link><description>
Sweden's centre-left opposition has defeated the incumbent right-wing governing bloc by the slimmest of margins, public broadcaster ​SVT ‌said on Wednesday, after 99% ⁠of the votes in Sunday's parliamentary election had been counted. FRANCE 24's Paul Rhys reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/426d5f8a-b202-11f1-9f67-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-203750-204158-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/426d5f8a-b202-11f1-9f67-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-203750-204158-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">47d28a54-b202-11f1-b1fb-6bfd10007bd4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:21:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>The 28th state? Carney's Canada draws closer to European Union</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260916-the-28th-state-carney-s-canada-draws-closer-to-european-union</link><description>
With a US president who talks of making Canada the 51st state, its leader in Europe where it’s not quite the EU's 28th state on offer, but something the president of the European Commission is calling ‘associate membership’. We’ll ask what that means, how it differs from the close status afforded to the likes of Iceland, Norway, Switzerland and the UK which Carney’s also visiting ahead of his own Strasbourg speech Thursday before the European Parliament. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3d723f5c-b1e2-11f1-88cf-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T083628Z-570247194-RC28KNAPX2ZW-RTRMADP-3-EU-PARLIAMENT-CARNEY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3d723f5c-b1e2-11f1-88cf-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T083628Z-570247194-RC28KNAPX2ZW-RTRMADP-3-EU-PARLIAMENT-CARNEY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2e803d2-b1f8-11f1-9a1e-7d47b0bed310</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:19:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ivorian footballer Malick Yalcouyé falsely accused of lying about his age</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-ivorian-footballer-malick-yalcouy%C3%A9-falsely-accused-of-lying-about-his-age</link><description>
During a Premier League match between Chelsea and Brighton, social media users started spreading rumours that 20-year-old Ivorian footballer Malick Yalcouyé is older than he claims to be. The rumours gained such proportion that the youth club where he trained decided to post photos of Yalcouyé throughout the years. Recently, similar accusations were made against the new Real Madrid striker Yan Diomandé.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faf0d2e8-a600-11f1-8e82-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-17.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faf0d2e8-a600-11f1-8e82-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-17.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43292096-b1ce-11f1-a567-2521ed09eebd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:03:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faf0d2e8-a600-11f1-8e82-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-17.png">© Premier League</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Former Kosovo president sentenced to 25 years for war crimes</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-former-kosovo-president-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes</link><description>
Former Kosovo President Hashim Thaci was found guilty of war crimes committed as part of the Kosovo Liberation Army including murder, torture and illegal arrests by a tribunal in The Hague on Wednesday. Thaci was sentenced to 25 ​years in prison alongside fellow former KLA figures who were also found guilty and sentenced.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffb01620-b1c9-11f1-8b3a-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CK27L.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffb01620-b1c9-11f1-8b3a-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CK27L.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">977d0508-b1ca-11f1-aed3-cdcd2ee68797</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:55:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffb01620-b1c9-11f1-8b3a-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CK27L.jpg">© Koen Van Weel, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU chief invites Canada to be first-ever ‘associate member’</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-eu-chief-pitches-associate-member-status-for-canada-as-both-seek-to-pivot-away-from-us</link><description>
EU chief Ursula von der Leyen raised the possibility on Wednesday that Canada could become the European Union’s first “associate member” during the annual State of the European Union speech, at which Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney was present. Carney has been pursuing closer ties with the EU as both seek to pivot away from the US.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d19923a-b1e9-11f1-a594-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259438375621.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d19923a-b1e9-11f1-a594-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259438375621.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3c3e830c-b1c9-11f1-89e6-c11fd12378d9</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:22:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d19923a-b1e9-11f1-a594-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259438375621.jpg">© Justin Tang, The Canadian Press via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russian drone attack on bus kills five in Ukraine's southeast</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-russian-drone-attack-on-bus-kills-five-in-ukraine-s-southeast</link><description>
Five people were killed and at least seven more were injured in a Russian drone attack on a passenger bus near the frontline in Ukraine's southeast on Wednesday, the regional governor said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32a17336-b19c-11f1-8958-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T064924Z-1003482524-RC24KNARF2CC-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32a17336-b19c-11f1-8958-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T064924Z-1003482524-RC24KNARF2CC-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29a8cc46-b19e-11f1-9784-83dc54a6a266</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 07:37:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32a17336-b19c-11f1-8958-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T064924Z-1003482524-RC24KNARF2CC-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Alina Smutko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU chief calls for creation of ‘European Security Council’, backs partnership with Canada</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-live-eu-chief-ursula-von-der-leyen-gives-state-of-the-union-address</link><description>
EU chief Ursula von der Leyen called for the creation of a "European Security Council", with countries including Britain and Ukraine, in her State of the European Union speech to the European Parliament in Strasbourg on Wednesday. Addressing this year's special guest, Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney, von der Leyen said she wants to open the door for Canada to become the bloc's first associate member.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efea9014-b19f-11f1-97b8-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T071848Z-60195985-RC27KNAAFBWQ-RTRMADP-3-EU-STATEOFUNION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efea9014-b19f-11f1-97b8-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T071848Z-60195985-RC27KNAAFBWQ-RTRMADP-3-EU-STATEOFUNION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9d5ff98-b13e-11f1-be36-99ae0684f658</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 05:20:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efea9014-b19f-11f1-97b8-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T071848Z-60195985-RC27KNAAFBWQ-RTRMADP-3-EU-STATEOFUNION.jpg">© Yves Herman, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France stalls EU Russia sanctions renewal over oligarch de-listing</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/france-stalls-eu-russia-sanctions-renewal-over-oligarch-de-listing</link><description>
European Union envoys have pushed back the expiry of EU Russia sanctions listings by ​seven days until September 22, a spokesperson for the EU's Irish presidency said on Monday, after failing to agree on a six-month renewal. At issue is whether to de-list Russian-Uzbek billionaire Alisher Usmanov. France has joined ​Slovakia in ‌a call to remove him, citing national security concerns, EU diplomats ⁠said. FRANCE 24's August Hakansson reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ba60012-b14e-11f1-aeb9-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-233414-233553-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ba60012-b14e-11f1-aeb9-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-233414-233553-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9185af8c-b14e-11f1-82a8-4110d51070be</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 21:46:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>NATO jets down drone over Lithuania as Russian ship fires flares at Danish helicopter</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-nato-jets-down-drone-over-lithuania-as-russian-ship-fires-flares-at-danish-helicopter</link><description>
NATO fighter jets shot down a drone that entered Lithuanian airspace and Denmark accused a Russian frigate of firing flares at a Danish military helicopter on Tuesday, in incidents that heightened tensions along the alliance’s eastern flank.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70fb22aa-b140-11f1-9cce-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T134257Z-1149854285-RC2OJNA2GC74-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE-MINISTERS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70fb22aa-b140-11f1-9cce-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T134257Z-1149854285-RC2OJNA2GC74-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE-MINISTERS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">79e24a4c-b140-11f1-a3b3-e9d99f3fc73c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:26:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70fb22aa-b140-11f1-9cce-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T134257Z-1149854285-RC2OJNA2GC74-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE-MINISTERS.jpg">© Janis Laizans, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Analysts call for step-up in response to Russia after Denmark, Lithuania incidents</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/analysts-call-for-step-up-in-response-to-russia-after-denmark-lithuania-incidents</link><description>
The European Union accused Russia on Tuesday of the "reckless" firing of flares at a Danish frigate which, with the shooting down of a drone over Lithuania, heightened the continent's anxiety over the Ukraine-Russia war. Danish analysts are calling for NATO and the EU to step up their response to Russia, according to FRANCE 24's Copenhagen correspondent Trine Villemann.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e5eaaa38-b139-11f1-9937-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-203356-203643-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e5eaaa38-b139-11f1-9937-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-203356-203643-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb7f7fd2-b139-11f1-96ea-b9649202be76</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:23:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Paris ex-mayor says 'collective failure' led to abuse of children in school care</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-paris-ex-mayor-says-collective-failure-led-to-abuse-of-children-in-school-care</link><description>
Former Paris mayor Anne Hidalgo acknowledged a “collective failure” to protect children on Tuesday as police investigate more than 200 allegations of violence, mistreatment and sexual abuse at the French capital’s state-run nurseries and primary schools for over more than a decade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/660460fe-b114-11f1-a509-e536a2be234a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8DA6CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/660460fe-b114-11f1-a509-e536a2be234a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8DA6CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d2990da-b114-11f1-880c-4d330ea93e7c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 15:27:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/660460fe-b114-11f1-a509-e536a2be234a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8DA6CQ.jpg">© Senate, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>NATO downs drone over Lithuania</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-nato-fighter-jets-shoot-down-drone-over-lithuania-after-latest-incursion</link><description>
NATO scrambled fighter jets overnight to ​shoot down a drone over Lithuania after the latest incursion on the alliance's eastern flank. In a separate incident, Denmark said a Russian warship fired two emergency flares at a Danish helicopter in the Baltic Sea, adding that the Russian ambassador had been summoned over the "reckless action". Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e289a39e-b111-11f1-ae2a-9bb98dcbfc77/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T081301Z-1741826540-RC2KJNASG13L-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e289a39e-b111-11f1-ae2a-9bb98dcbfc77/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T081301Z-1741826540-RC2KJNASG13L-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7ae271c-b0ab-11f1-9bc0-97b5e2715bc5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 02:19:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e289a39e-b111-11f1-ae2a-9bb98dcbfc77/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T081301Z-1741826540-RC2KJNASG13L-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE.jpg">© Lithuanian army, Reuters </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky says Ukraine ready to de-escalate if Russia halts strikes</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-zelensky-says-ukraine-ready-to-de-escalate-if-russia-halts-strikes</link><description>
Ukraine is ready to halt attacks on Russian energy infrastructure if Moscow does the same, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday, after US President Donald Trump announced an apparent agreement between the two sides. Kyiv also warned that intensifying Russian strikes on Ukraine’s rail network are worsening each week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/183b4120-b084-11f1-9cad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239577216137.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/183b4120-b084-11f1-9cad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239577216137.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a838820a-b08f-11f1-b656-b3452f437d0f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:57:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/183b4120-b084-11f1-9cad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239577216137.jpg">© Aurel Obreja, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>'The very existence of LGBTQI people is seen as obscene', Turkish activist says</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260914-the-very-existence-of-lgbtqi-people-is-seen-as-obscene-turkish-activist-says</link><description>
Turkish police on Sunday swooped into gay bars and the homes of LGBTQ activists, arresting at least 60 people in raids authorities said were aimed at boosting traditional family values, officials and activists said. Turkey's LGBTQ community has frequently been targeted by the government, with President Recep Tayyip Erdogan labelling it as a "deviant movement" of "perverts" responsible for the falling birth rate. In this edition, FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Yildiz Tar, Editor-in-Chief of KaosGL.org.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bb447d6-b07e-11f1-b32d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-223110-224619-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bb447d6-b07e-11f1-b32d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-223110-224619-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a5ebc17a-b07f-11f1-82d6-69c181e861bd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:02:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Monte FRANCIS</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Dozens arrested in major anti-LGBTQ raids in Turkey</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/dozens-arrested-in-major-anti-lgbtq-raids-in-turkey</link><description>
