Twelve European countries meeting in Finland on Monday urged the European Union to beef up its presence in the Arctic, a geopolitical battleground caught between Russia and US President Donald Trump. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a70e00e8-077b-11f1-9159-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-01-21T100746Z-426063708-RC2Q9T9RM703-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-GREENLAND-ARCTIC-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a70e00e8-077b-11f1-9159-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-01-21T100746Z-426063708-RC2Q9T9RM703-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-GREENLAND-ARCTIC-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6c26be16-b06d-11f1-84d9-f7a544c1e209</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:06:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Leaders urge EU to expand Arctic presence amid Russia 'threat'</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-leaders-urge-eu-to-expand-arctic-presence-amid-russia-threat</link><description>
Twelve European countries on Monday called for the European Union to step up its presence in the Arctic, as melting ice opens new maritime routes while growing tensions with Russia and the United States increasingly put the region in the geopolitical spotlight.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3e7efa6-b05d-11f1-8f77-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-14T083344Z-28794335-RC2WINAMRIJJ-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ARCTIC-FINLAND.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3e7efa6-b05d-11f1-8f77-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-14T083344Z-28794335-RC2WINAMRIJJ-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ARCTIC-FINLAND.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bef25b04-b05f-11f1-a490-f3183e9ef446</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:41:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3e7efa6-b05d-11f1-8f77-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-14T083344Z-28794335-RC2WINAMRIJJ-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ARCTIC-FINLAND.jpg">© Jouni Porsanger via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Sweden faces political uncertainty after knife-edge election</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-sweden-faces-political-uncertainty-after-knife-edge-election</link><description>
Sweden was bracing for a protracted struggle to form a government on Monday after election results showed a thin and uncertain lead for the left-wing opposition, while the far-right Sweden Democrats lost ground for the first time since entering parliament 16 years ago.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30a95848-b01e-11f1-a802-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/b28430f58cc3264b2403477f397ab356b8bdf8d4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30a95848-b01e-11f1-a802-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/b28430f58cc3264b2403477f397ab356b8bdf8d4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31b15bfa-b01e-11f1-9856-f30fc234c655</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 09:25:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30a95848-b01e-11f1-a802-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/b28430f58cc3264b2403477f397ab356b8bdf8d4.jpg">© Jonathan Nackstrand, AFP  </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Sweden Election Aftermath: A hard night for the hard right?</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-sweden-election-aftermath-a-hard-night-for-the-hard-right</link><description>
FRANCE 24’s Gavin Lee speaks to Scandinavia Correspondent Trine Villeman for some analysis on how Sweden has voted in the 2026 election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84572cd0-af39-11f1-afd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7XT2GD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84572cd0-af39-11f1-afd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7XT2GD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">968803b4-afa4-11f1-a9ff-7b8ae3515f31</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:04:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Sweden's centre-left holds razor-thin edge as exit polls show tight race</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-leads-election-as-far-right-slips-exit-polls-show</link><description>
Sweden's general election remained too close to call early Monday, with nearly 90 percent of votes counted. Four opposition parties led by Social Democrat Magdalena Andersson held a one-seat parliamentary lead over Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson's right-wing bloc, which includes the Sweden Democrats, as both leaders said they were ready to govern.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b6a890ec-af9e-11f1-80aa-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T175249Z-1939019679-RC2HINAXGOPT-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b6a890ec-af9e-11f1-80aa-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T175249Z-1939019679-RC2HINAXGOPT-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3da4af80-afa0-11f1-aa6e-1122ecf5d05d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 18:25:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b6a890ec-af9e-11f1-80aa-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T175249Z-1939019679-RC2HINAXGOPT-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg">© Denis Balibouse, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine, Poland condemn Russia after drone strikes train near border</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-poland-ukraine-slam-russian-strikes-near-border-as-escalation</link><description>
Ukraine and Poland on Sunday condemned Russian strikes close to the Polish border as an "escalation" in the war, after drones struck a Warsaw-bound train. Ukraine's rail operator said former British PM Boris Johnson and ex-US CIA director David Petraeus were at a border train station nearby around the time the train was hit.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4663a8c-afaa-11f1-a871-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8868T3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4663a8c-afaa-11f1-a871-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8868T3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d313a32c-af9c-11f1-8fa6-8db889befaf6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:59:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4663a8c-afaa-11f1-a871-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8868T3.jpg">© Ukrainian State Emergency Service via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sweden: Tight election puts all eyes on the far right</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/sweden-tight-election-puts-all-eyes-on-the-far-right</link><description>
Swedes are voting in a closely fought general election that could see the far-right Sweden Democrats enter government for the first time. With immigration, crime and the economy dominating the campaign, Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson and Social Democrat leader Magdalena Andersson are locked in a neck-and-neck race.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ebf82fc-af89-11f1-86a8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-171154-171339-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ebf82fc-af89-11f1-86a8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-171154-171339-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a3efd90c-af89-11f1-848c-1d982ffe8823</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:55:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Swedish far-right eyes role in government</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/swedish-far-right-eyes-role-in-government</link><description>
As Sweden heads into a closely fought election, the far right is gaining ground by tapping into concerns over crime and security, issues that some voters increasingly associate with migration. On FRANCE 24, Stockholm University sociologist Zeth Isaksson said the movement has also softened its image in recent years, making it more acceptable to a broader electorate, while also cautioning against overstating the strength of the far right in Sweden.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d325c64-af53-11f1-8d54-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20799631186aa669301c83e0-07656090.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d325c64-af53-11f1-8d54-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20799631186aa669301c83e0-07656090.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9efc97ae-af71-11f1-a226-7db7cf189a1f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:11:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sweden election: A turning point for the far right?</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/sweden-election-a-turning-point-for-the-far-right</link><description>
The stakes are high in Sweden's general election, with the far right poised to enter government for the first time. TV4 News journalist Markus Karlsson-Bourrioux explains how opinion polls shifted from a comfortable centre-left lead to a tight race over the summer, and how far-right ideas have gained ground since the last election in 2022.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/426517d8-af57-11f1-b8a8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-110343-110655-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/426517d8-af57-11f1-b8a8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-110343-110655-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">470ce630-af57-11f1-9a1a-e5cb8c8e2679</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:48:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany: Thousands rally against far-right after AfD victory</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/germany-thousands-rally-against-far-right-after-afd-victory</link><description>
Tens of thousands of people marched in around 20 cities across Germany to protest the rise of the far right after the AfD's historic victory in the Saxony-Anhalt state election. Demonstrators said they were defending democracy as mainstream parties continue to rule out governing with the AfD.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b94b4a34-af4d-11f1-9e44-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-100840-101014-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b94b4a34-af4d-11f1-9e44-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-100840-101014-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">be44bef8-af4d-11f1-a7d9-892c781611bd</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:41:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Swedes vote in close general election that could usher far right into government</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-swedes-vote-in-close-general-election-that-could-usher-far-right-into-government</link><description>
Swedes are heading to the polls Sunday for a general election that will either bring a far right party into government for the first time or shift the country back towards the liberalism it has long been known for. The centre-left opposition holds a narrow lead over the ruling right-wing bloc but Prime ⁠Minister Ulf Kristersson's four-party alliance – which includes the far right Sweden Democrats – has been catching up in the final weeks of campaigning.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84572cd0-af39-11f1-afd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7XT2GD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84572cd0-af39-11f1-afd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7XT2GD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">033aa45a-af3a-11f1-a91a-0529a93c31a8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 06:16:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84572cd0-af39-11f1-afd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7XT2GD.jpg">© Jonathan Nackstrand, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Tens of thousands protest against far-right AfD party in Germany</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-tens-of-thousands-of-people-protest-in-germany-against-far-right-afd</link><description>
About 150,000 demonstrators took to the streets in around 20 cities across Germany on Saturday against the far-right AfD, after the party scored a crushing victory in a state election last week. The Alternative for Germany (AfD) topped the vote in the eastern region of Saxony-Anhalt, and is now seeking to form the first extreme-right state government in Germany since World War II.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83bf7692-aecb-11f1-b02e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84J6TY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83bf7692-aecb-11f1-b02e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84J6TY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">17cdd6f2-aecd-11f1-a593-59a4b5cc5e30</guid><pubDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:12:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83bf7692-aecb-11f1-b02e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84J6TY.jpg">© Ralf Hirschberger, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
